1. Enables stack monitoring using `setMonitoringEnabled(true)`
2. Initializes the stack monitor with `initialize()`
3. Gets initial usage statistics with `getUsageStats()`
4. Checks template-based allocation with `canAllocate<1024>()`
5. Checks runtime allocation with `canAllocate(1024)`
6. Creates a large `StackGuard` instance (half the max limit to ensure success)
7. Checks if the guard was successfully created with `success()`
8. Tests if additional allocation would be blocked while guard is held
9. Gets usage statistics while the guard is active
10. Returns the snapshot (guard destructor will clean up automatically)

