Looking at the requirements and the code fragments, I need to implement a function that tests Resource<Void> behavior. Let me analyze the key aspects:

1. Resource<Void> - a resource holding Void type
2. Check SBO (Small Buffer Optimization) storage
3. Get value and verify it's Void
4. Use ObserverGraph to register/name/close nodes
5. Return a snapshot with the test results

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#pragma once

#include <reaction/core/resource.h>
#include <reaction/graph/observer_graph.h>
#include <memory>
#include <string>
#include <type_traits>

namespace test_reaction {

struct VoidResourceSnapshot {
    bool retrievedIsVoid;
    bool usesSboStorage;
    bool nameAssigned;
    bool nameClearedAfterClose;
};

inline VoidResourceSnapshot test_resource_void_behavior(const std::string &nodeName) {
    VoidResourceSnapshot snapshot{};

    // 1. Create shared Resource<Void> instance
    auto voidResource = std::make_shared<reaction::Resource<reaction::Void>>();

    // 2. Check if resource uses SBO storage
    snapshot.usesSboStorage = voidResource->usesSboStorage();

    // 3. Get value from resource
    auto retrievedValue = voidResource->get();

    // 4. Check if retrieved value is Void type
    snapshot.retrievedIsVoid = std::is_same_v<decltype(retrievedValue), reaction::Void>;

    // 5. Get observer graph instance
    auto &graph = reaction::ObserverGraph::getInstance();

    // 6. Register resource node
    auto nodePtr = voidResource->getPtr();
    graph.addNode(nodePtr);

    // 7. Assign node name
    graph.setName(nodePtr, nodeName);

    // 8. Check if name was assigned
    std::string assignedName = graph.getName(nodePtr);
    snapshot.nameAssigned = (assignedName == nodeName);

    // 9. Close node
    graph.closeNode(nodePtr);

    // 10. Check if name was cleared after close
    std::string nameAfterClose = graph.getName(nodePtr);
    snapshot.nameClearedAfterClose = nameAfterClose.empty();

    // 11. Return void resource snapshot
    return snapshot;
}

}  // namespace test_reaction
```

This implementation:
1. Creates a shared Resource<Void> instance
2. Checks if it uses Small Buffer Optimization (SBO) storage
3. Retrieves the value from the resource
4. Verifies at compile-time that the retrieved value is of Void type
5. Gets the singleton ObserverGraph instance
6. Registers the resource node with the graph
7. Assigns the provided name to the node
8. Verifies the name was correctly assigned by retrieving it
9. Closes the node (which should cascade and clean up)
10. Checks that the name was cleared after closing (part of cleanup)
11. Returns a snapshot containing all the test results

